# HATS — seasonal hats worn on a per-frame head anchor (see SPEC.md "Looks and hats").
# Each hat is centred on the pixel BOUNDARY x = 8 (cols 7|8), mirror-symmetric except a
# deliberate flourish. Row 15 is the row that sits ON the fox's head (it covers the head's
# top outline between the ears); everything else is above it. At most 10 px wide
# (cols 3-12) and 8 px tall (rows 8-15). Hats are never recoloured by a look.

# New Year: blue cone tapering in three tiers (6/4/2 px, no k outline, which vanishes on
# black), two yellow stripes, white pom-pom. It ends on a blue row so the hat's bottom edge
# stays crisp against the fox's y head highlight.
@frame hat_party
